# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# On Windows, `core.autocrlf` rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For a shell
# script that corrupts the shebang — the interpreter path becomes `/bin/sh\r`,
# and the script fails with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
#
# For the git hooks that means failing *open*, silently: the hook does not run,
# and a secret-scanning hook that quietly stops scanning is worse than none, on
# exactly the platform this repo is developed on.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# For the container entrypoint the same rewrite is what makes an image built on
# Windows crash-loop on Render with `exec ./docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file
# or directory` — pointing at a file that is plainly right there in the image.
backend/docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
